1810   DB66             ;* Adds a new thread to the VM. The data for this routine is contained 
1811   DB66             ;* directly after the jsr to this routine. A single byte follows the
1812   DB66             ;* jsr and is the timer byte used for the delay until the thread starts.
1813   DB66             ;* The actual address directly after the timer byte is where the thread
1814   DB66             ;* will start running. Example:
1815   DB66             ;*
1816   DB66             ;*  jsr addthread
1817   DB66             ;*    .db 05        ;This is the timer byte
1818   DB66             ;*  ldaa #FF        ;This code is executed as the thread.
