3577   E44F             
3578   E44F             ;This is unused in the macros. You must call it directly at $F1D5
3579   E44F             ;The behavior of this command is probably the most complex. It 
3580   E44F             ;starts at the last lamp in the range. If it is already set, then
3581   E44F             ;the routine simply exits. If the last lamp is not set, the routine
3582   E44F             ;goes down through each lamp in the range. If if finds a lamp on,
3583   E44F             ;then it turns off that lamp, then goes back up to the next lamp
3584   E44F             ;and turns it on. If no lamps are on in the range, then the first
3585   E44F             ;lamp in the range is turned on.
3586   E44F             ;The best example of this routine is for the 10-20-30 lamps on 
3587   E44F             ;Jungle Lord. It will simply incrment the 10-20-30 lamps sequentially
3588   E44F             ;and then stop at 30. If none are on, then it will turn on 10.
3589   E44F             lampm_g             
3590   E44F 8D 4F                       bsr lampr_end               ;A = Last Lamp Level, B = Last Lamp BitPos
3591   E451 26 3A                       bne abx_ret
